{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Our Beginning (Our Story band 2)

  A fork of sections/sh-story-split.liquid, not a replacement for it. The generic
  section stays on disk and stays on its old [data-reveal] entrance; this file
  exists so band 2 and band 4 can carry the §28 motion contract without dragging
  every other possible instance of a story split onto it.

  IT KEEPS THE CLASS .sh-split. That is the whole point of forking rather than
  rewriting: every line of the resting design — the grid, the feather, the
  mirrored columns, the light-surface colour trio, the <=767px stack — is
  shudhi-home.css §18 and is reused verbatim. .sh-split--beginning is a hook for
  nothing today; it exists so a future band-2-only rule has somewhere to go
  without reaching for an id.

  WHAT CHANGED FROM THE GENERIC, AND WHY

  1. [data-reveal] IS GONE from .sh-split__copy. It carried `opacity: 0` from
     shudhi-home.css §4 via a bare attribute, so a thrown exception, a 404 or a
     blocked script left a photograph with no words next to it. Every pre-state now
     sits behind .is-armed, which assets/sh-story-motion.js only ever writes when
     it already holds the observer that clears it.
     The orphaned rules at §18 (.sh-split__copy[data-reveal] and its three
     nth-child delays) are deliberately NOT deleted — sh-story-split.liquid still
     ships and still emits the attribute. They simply never match on this page.

  2. .sh-split__frame is new, and its `position: absolute; inset: 0` is
     LOAD-BEARING rather than styling. shudhi-home.js:374 reads
     `pxEls[i].parentNode.getBoundingClientRect()` to drive the scroll parallax,
     and after this change that parent is the frame. Inset:0 inside the
     position:relative media box makes it exactly congruent with the box the
     parallax used to measure, so the effect is unchanged. Make it a plain in-flow
     div and the photo's containing block silently reverts — the layout still
     looks right while parallax measures a zero-height parent and skips the
     element, which presents as "the parallax stopped working" with nothing in the
     CSS to point at.

  3. NO botanical motif, NO paper grain, NO light drift. All three were designed
     and all three are cut: each would be a NEW element present in the resting
     picture, and the brief's first rule is that the page at rest is the reference.
     Motion may reveal this composition; it may not add to it.

  4. NO pointer depth. The photo already carries 15px of scroll parallax, and a
     second transform system on the same band buys ~3px nobody asked for.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'shudhi-story.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}

<section class="sh sh-split sh-split--beginning"
         {%- if s.anchor_id != blank %} id="{{ s.anchor_id | handle }}"{% endif -%}
         {%- if s.animate %} data-sh-reveal{% endif %}
         data-media-position="{{ s.media_position }}"
         style="--sh-split-bg:{{ s.bg }};--sh-split-h:{{ s.min_height }}px;--sh-lead:180ms;">

  <div class="sh-split__grid">

    <div class="sh-split__media">
      {%- if s.image != blank -%}
        {%- assign img_h = 1400 | divided_by: s.image.aspect_ratio | round -%}
        {%- comment -%} The settle rides the frame; the parallax rides the photo. One
            transform job per element, so neither can overwrite the other. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sh-split__frame">
          <img class="sh-split__photo"{% if s.animate %} data-parallax{% endif %}
               src="{{ s.image | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
               alt="{{ s.image.alt | escape }}"
               width="1400" height="{{ img_h }}"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%} No photo picked in the editor yet — fall back to the bundled
            botanical asset so the band never ships a blank panel. Same frame + photo
            structure as the branch above: the settle rides the frame, the parallax
            rides the photo. A photo picked in the theme editor still wins. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sh-split__frame">
          <img class="sh-split__photo"{% if s.animate %} data-parallax{% endif %}
               src="{{ 'automflower.png' | asset_url }}"
               alt=""
               width="2048" height="768"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="sh-split__copy">

      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="sh-split__eyebrow sh-eyebrow" data-sh-fade style="--i:0">{{ s.eyebrow }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h2 class="sh-split__title sh-serif" data-sh-fade style="--i:1">
        {{ s.heading }}{% if s.heading_em != blank %} <em>{{ s.heading_em }}</em>{% endif %}
      </h2>

      {%- if s.body != blank -%}
        <p class="sh-split__text" data-sh-fade style="--i:2">{{ s.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Both halves required. A label with no destination used to fall
          back to href="#", and an empty fragment means "top of the document" — so a
          reader who reached this band and pressed the link was thrown back to the
          hero, losing their place with no announcement (WCAG 2.4.4). Hiding the
          link is the honest failure mode; a dead one is not. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.link_label != blank and s.link_url != blank -%}
        <a class="sh-split__link sh-btn sh-btn--ghost" href="{{ s.link_url }}" data-sh-fade style="--i:3">
          {{ s.link_label }} {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{%- if s.animate -%}
  <script src="{{ 'sh-story-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Story — Beginning",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our Beginning" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Headline" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The heading is split in two: the plain part, then the tail shown in gold italic." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "From tradition to" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading_em", "label": "Heading — gold italic tail", "default": "today." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body text", "default": "Our journey began with time-honored herbal rituals passed down through four generations. Inspired by ancient wisdom and family practices, we create products that bring balance and well-being to modern lives." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_label", "label": "Link label",
      "info": "Set this and the URL below together — neither renders on its own." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link_url", "label": "Link URL",
      "info": "The link stays hidden until this is set — a labelled link with no destination jumps the reader back to the top of the page." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Media" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image",
      "info": "Full-bleed to the viewport edge on its side. The bundled blossom artwork stands in until one is picked — a photo chosen here replaces it." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "media_position", "label": "Image side", "default": "left",
      "info": "Below 768px the image is always shown first, whichever side is chosen.",
      "options": [ { "value": "left", "label": "Left" }, { "value": "right", "label": "Right" } ] },
    { "type": "range", "id": "min_height", "label": "Band height", "min": 380, "max": 760, "step": 20, "default": 520, "unit": "px" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor_id", "label": "Anchor id",
      "info": "Optional. Lets another section link straight to this band with #your-id. Must be unique on the page." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "animate", "label": "Animate on scroll", "default": true,
      "info": "Turns off the copy entrance and the photo's scroll drift together. The band still renders in full." },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#f6ede1",
      "info": "The panel colour, and the colour the photo's inner edge feathers into. Keep it light — the heading, body and link colours are tuned for a light surface." }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
